                    <div class="section-num">06 / FAQs</div>
                    <h2 style="margin-top:6px;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                    <p class="sub">Quick answers on validity, recognition, and choosing the right program.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-wrap" id="faqList">
                <div class="faq-item">
                    <button class="faq-q">Are online and distance degrees valid in India? <span class="plus">+</span></button>
                    <div class="faq-a">Yes. They are valid and legally recognized in India when offered by UGC-approved universities as per UGC–DEB guidelines.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="faq-item">
                    <button class="faq-q">Are online degrees accepted by HRs and companies? <span class="plus">+</span></button>
                    <div class="faq-a">Most private companies, MNCs, startups and corporate organizations accept online degrees, provided they're from a recognized, reputed university.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="faq-item">
                    <button class="faq-q">Are online degrees equivalent to regular degrees? <span class="plus">+</span></button>
                    <div class="faq-a">Yes. As per UGC norms, online and distance degrees are equivalent to regular degrees in curriculum, credit structure and certification.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="faq-item">
                    <button class="faq-q">Can I get a job after completing an online degree? <span class="plus">+</span></button>
                    <div class="faq-a">Absolutely. Holders are employed across IT, Banking &amp; Finance, Marketing, HR, and Data &amp; Analytics — outcomes depend on skills, specialization, internships and project experience.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="faq-item">
                    <button class="faq-q">Are online degrees accepted for government jobs? <span class="plus">+</span></button>
                    <div class="faq-a">Degrees from UGC-approved universities are accepted for many government jobs, subject to the specific recruitment authority's eligibility criteria.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="faq-item">
                    <button class="faq-q">Can I pursue higher studies after an online degree? <span class="plus">+</span></button>
                    <div class="faq-a">Yes — Master's programs after UG, PhD programs after PG, and professional certifications in India or abroad, subject to university admission criteria.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="faq-item">
                    <button class="faq-q">Do online degrees mention "online" on the certificate? <span class="plus">+</span></button>
                    <div class="faq-a">No. Most universities issue the same degree certificate as regular programs, without mentioning the mode of study.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="faq-item">
                    <button class="faq-q">Who should opt for online or distance education? <span class="plus">+</span></button>
                    <div class="faq-a">Working professionals, fresh graduates, career switchers, entrepreneurs, and students preparing for competitive exams.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="faq-item">
                    <button class="faq-q">How do HRs verify online degrees? <span class="plus">+</span></button>
                    <div class="faq-a">Through university enrollment numbers, UGC-approved university databases, digital verification portals, and transcripts/marksheets.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="faq-item">
                    <button class="faq-q">Are online degrees accepted abroad? <span class="plus">+</span></button>
                    <div class="faq-a">Many international employers and universities accept online degrees from reputed Indian universities, though acceptance varies by country and institution.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="faq-item">
                    <button class="faq-q">Are online programs easier than regular programs? <span class="plus">+</span></button>
                    <div class="faq-a">No. Online programs follow the same academic standards, assessments and examinations as regular programs.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="faq-item">
                    <button class="faq-q">How does SkillBridge help students choose the right program? <span class="plus">+</span></button>
                    <div class="faq-a">SkillBridge provides unbiased counselling to help students choose UGC-approved universities, select career-oriented specializations, and avoid unrecognized institutions.</div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>



